---
import { href } from '../../lib/site';

const commands = `git clone https://github.com/iamkallolpratim/ai-gov.git && cd ai-gov
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build`;
---

<section id="quickstart" class="alt">
  <div class="wrap grid two">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Quickstart</p>
      <h2>Three commands, then open localhost:3000</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        You need Docker with Compose v2. On first boot the API migrates the database, seeds four
        jurisdictions, the policy packs and four example AI systems, and loads the policies into OPA.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sign in as <code>admin@aigov.example.com</code> with password <code>ChangeMe123!</code>. These
        are public development credentials, and the server refuses to start in staging or
        production while they are still in place.
      </p>
      <p><a href={href('docs/quickstart/')}>Full quickstart →</a> · <a href={href('docs/self-hosting/')}>Self-hosting →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="term">
      <pre class="code"><code>{commands}</code></pre>
      <table class="ports">
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Console</td><td><code>http://localhost:3000</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>API docs</td><td><code>http://localhost:8000/docs</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Readiness</td><td><code>http://localhost:8000/ready</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .term {
    align-self: center;
  }
  .ports {
    min-width: 0;
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .ports td {
    padding: 6px 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .ports td:first-child {
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 110px;
  }
</style>
